@@@!atrep

@@/ at-epimerismos: the parsing pack (ἐπιμερισμός, the Byzantine
@@/ schoolroom's word-by-word grammatical parsing of a text: for
@@/ each word its lemma, its part of speech, its accidents) -
@@/ token-level linguistic annotation, the layer corpora and
@@/ treebanks carry: the Russian National Corpus, OpenCorpora,
@@/ PROIEL, TEI's w element, Strong's-tagged scripture.
@@/ Like at-aphanes, every sim is a monosim, so litosis strips the
@@/ whole pack; unlike at-aphanes it needs a span for every word,
@@/ and that span must not enter the text's identity either. The
@@/ span is therefore the endo-diaphane, the transparent wrapper
@@/ litosis unwraps and kanonizo keeps only while it carries
@@/ something - an onym, a genos, or (this pack's case) an
@@/ annotation monosim written first inside it:
@@/
@@/   @@.@!=(школа)@!/(S)@!%(f,inan=sg,nom)Школа.@@
@@/
@@/ is a token: the parsing first, then the form. Several
@@/ parsings (an ambiguous token) repeat from lexema. A sentence
@@/ is an endo-diaphane opened by the periodos marker, holding
@@/ its tokens and the untokenized text between them; when
@@/ syntax points from token to token (PROIEL heads), the tokens
@@/ carry onyms and kephale points at them (kanonizo keeps the
@@/ referenced ones and renumbers both sides); a citation
@@/ coordinate that changes between tokens is a core milestone.
@@/ An annotated text and the bare text have the same litos: the
@@/ parsing is analysis, not text.
@@/ Values are free tokens in the source's own tagset (RNC's gr,
@@/ OpenCorpora's grammemes, PROIEL's morphology code): the pack
@@/ carries the analysis, it does not translate it.
@@/ Part of the standard library; composes with koine and its
@@/ sibling packs.

@=== periodos
@!.(id)
@"opens a sentence: the diaphane it heads is one sentence"@
@""
περίοδος, the sentence. Written first inside an endo-diaphane
that spans the sentence; the parameter is the source's sentence
id (OpenCorpora, PROIEL) or a running number. Tokens nest inside.
""@
===@

@=== lexema
@!=(lemma)
@"the lexeme the token belongs to, named by its lemma"@
@""
λέξημα. RNC ana/@lex, OpenCorpora l/@t, PROIEL token/@lemma, TEI
w/@lemma. Opens a parsing: a second lexema on the same token
opens a second, alternative parsing.
""@
===@

@=== meros
@!/(pos)
@"the part of speech (μέρος λόγου)"@
@""
The first item of an RNC gr string, the first grammeme of an
OpenCorpora analysis, PROIEL part-of-speech, TEI w/@pos.
""@
===@

@=== parepomena
@!%(features)
@"the accidents: the grammatical features beyond the part of speech"@
@""
Dionysius Thrax's παρεπόμενα - gender, number, case, tense, mood,
voice and the rest - in the source's own spelling: the remainder
of an RNC gr string (`f,inan=sg,nom`, keeping a leading `=` when
the string had one), OpenCorpora grammemes after the first, joined
with commas, PROIEL's morphology code, TEI w/@msd.
""@
===@

@=== semasia
@!&(class)
@"a semantic class of the lexeme"@
@""
σημασία. RNC ana/@sem; spaces in the source value are written as
underscores (a parameter carries no whitespace).
""@
===@

@=== kephale
@!>(onym)
@"the syntactic head: the onym of the token this one depends on"@
@""
κεφαλή. PROIEL head-id, any dependency treebank. Points at a token
diaphane's onym; kanonizo renumbers both together.
""@
===@

@=== schesis
@!-(relation)
@"the dependency relation to the head"@
@""
σχέσις. PROIEL relation (pred, sub, obj, ...), Universal
Dependencies deprel.
""@
===@
